generated_hash =

// @vibe/compiler/loader — ADR-0070 / #897 compiler-internal contract,
// compiler-internal batch 7. Module-graph loading: source collection off
// disk (collect_all_sources_fs / collect_source_groups_fs /
// collect_sources_rec), persistent list/group/manifest-header caching (the
// resolution_context_*, load_persistent_*, store_persistent_* families),
// contract/publish-bump plumbing (contract_package_hashes_fs,
// fill_require_pins_fs*, publish_check_fs), package-boundary enforcement
// (enforce_incoming_boundary_fs, validate_index_layout_fs, vpkg directory
// scanning), plus the tab-separated build manifest reader
// (manifest_sources.vibe) and its persistent header-scan cache
// (header_cache.vibe). Three files, no naming collision on the established
// `git mv index.vibe <dirname>.vibe` rename convention (unlike checker/'s
// and codegen/'s batches), so the old index.vibe moved verbatim to
// loader.vibe.
//
// loader.vibe is NOT a pure facade — like codegen/common_base's batch, it
// carries substantial real implementation of its own (source collection,
// caching, contract/publish helpers) in addition to importing and
// re-exporting a chosen subset of manifest_sources.vibe's surface. Its
// existing `export ./manifest_sources.vibe { .. }` SReExport block (added
// under #847, see its own comment in loader.vibe) stays untouched: this
// contract is now the actual source of truth for the package's full export
// surface (all 34 names below, across all 3 files), so the facade's
// partial, hand-picked re-export list is no longer load-bearing for
// outside callers — they reach every name here through this contract
// regardless of what loader.vibe itself re-exports, exactly like
// checker_facade.vibe's partial list after checker/'s batch.
//
// join_path naming wrinkle (the specific case #847 flagged this directory
// as a "facade-design blocker" over): loader.vibe defines its own PRIVATE,
// same-named `join_path` helper (a deliberate duplicate, see its own #740
// comment) — so loader.vibe can never itself
// `export ./manifest_sources.vibe { join_path }` without colliding with
// its own local binding, and manifest_sources.vibe's `join_path` was
// therefore unreachable through the old plain-index.vibe facade.
// loader_hotspot_probe.vibe worked around this with a documented direct
// leaf import straight from `loader/manifest_sources.vibe`. A .vpkg
// contract has no such collision: it declares bodyless signatures, not
// executable bindings, so `join_path` below (grouped under
// manifest_sources.vibe) declares the export cleanly. The workaround leaf
// import is retracted by this migration — loader_hotspot_probe.vibe now
// gets `join_path` the same way as every other manifest_sources.vibe
// export, through this contract's `import ../loader { .. }` package form.
//
// No exported types: TypeEnv/Stmt/Subst/Type (../core) and Map (builtin)
// are plain structural signature text here, not declared at all
// (normalize/perceus/contract precedent) — ../core itself was not yet
// migrated to vpkg at the time of this batch (out of scope then), so
// loader.vibe / header_cache.vibe kept their existing bare `import
// ../core/index.vibe { .. }` style references unchanged. #897 batch 9
// migrated core/ to its own index.vpkg and, per that contract's own
// boundary-enforcement note, converted these two literal leaf-path
// references to the bare `import ../core { .. }` package form (manifest_sources.vibe
// never imported this compiler-internal ../core — its `@vibe/core` import
// is the unrelated external stdlib package).
//
// External-caller fixes (literal `loader/index.vibe` /
// `loader/manifest_sources.vibe` / `loader/header_cache.vibe` paths → bare
// `../loader` / `./loader` package form, now that leaf-file imports from
// outside the package are rejected by enforce_incoming_boundary_fs):
// cli_adapter.vibe, loader_hotspot_probe.vibe (also folds its join_path
// workaround import into the package form), loader_list_materialize_bench.vibe,
// loader_materialize_bench.vibe, tests/contract_vpkg_test.vibe,
// tests/loader_manifest_sources_test.vibe,
// entry/source_compile/wasi_only/merge_sources.vibe,
// entry/compiler/file_compile/file_compile.vibe,
// entry/compiler/fs_compile/index.vibe. No import cycle found: none of
// loader/'s own dependencies (checker/, runtime/eval_loader/, contract/,
// syntax/ — all already vpkg) import back into loader/.
//
// Compiled into the compiler itself via compiler_sources_manifest.tsv
// (group `loader`): the old single `loader/index.vibe` row becomes a dual
// row (this contract + loader.vibe); header_cache.vibe and
// manifest_sources.vibe already had their own rows and are unchanged.

